// endpoint_forget_workspace.proto — ForgetWorkspace: remove a workspace's
// REGISTRY RECORD and touch nothing else. SIDEBAR section. It is the undo for
// a registration, and it is a THIRD thing beside the two verbs it is easily
// confused with:
//
//   - Close is reversible and keeps the record: the workspace leaves the tab
//     bar and Open brings it back.
//   - Nuke DESTROYS the worktree and the branch and then forgets the record.
//   - Forget deletes the record and leaves every file alone. The directory
//     survives, and re-registering it mints a fresh record.
//
// It exists because nothing else ever removed a registry record for a
// directory the user registered by hand, so the register-then-clean-up cycle
// left a workspace row (and its repository row) naming a path that may no
// longer be there.
//
// A FORGET STANDS THE SESSION DOWN FIRST, the way Nuke does: the row it
// resolves through is about to go, so this is the LAST verb that can address
// the workspace's shim.
//
// A FORGET REQUIRES A CLOSED WORKSPACE, and it cannot close one for the
// caller: the close verb owns the quiet requirement, and a close-then-forget
// would either duplicate that gate or bypass it — and bypassing it silently
// discards undelivered user intent. The refusal says so by name.

